<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://delicias.dia.fi.upm.es/ontologies/SimpleOrAggregated.owl#"
     xml:base="http://delicias.dia.fi.upm.es/ontologies/SimpleOrAggregated.owl"
     xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:owl2xml="http://www.w3.org/2006/12/owl2-xml#"
     xmlns:SimpleOrAggregated="http://delicias.dia.fi.upm.es/ontologies/SimpleOrAggregated.owl#"
     xmlns:cpannotationschema="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://delicias.dia.fi.upm.es/ontologies/SimpleOrAggregated.owl">
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl"/>
        <dc:creator>Mari Carmen Suárez Figueroa Baonza</dc:creator>
        <dc:creator>María Poveda</dc:creator>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The goal of this pattern is to represent objects that can be simple or aggregated (that is, several objects gathered in another object acting as a whole). The main difference between the aggregation relation and other mereological relationships (such as part of or composition) is that the aggregated object and its aggregated members should belong to the same concept. For example, a turbine is part of an engine, whereas an aggregated provider is formed by providers.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Simpleoraggregated Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>What elements are aggregated members of this object?</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>What is this object aggregated member of?</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>This Content OP allows designers to represent aggregations relations.</cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>
        <cpannotationschema:hasIntent>The goal of this pattern is to represent objects that can be simple or aggregated (that is, several objects gathered in another object acting as a whole). The main difference between the aggregation relation and other mereological relationships (such as part of or composition) is that the aggregated object and its aggregated members should belong to the same concept. For example, a turbine is part of an engine, whereas an aggregated provider is formed by providers. </cpannotationschema:hasIntent>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label trimmed x1; label moved to skos:prefLabel x8; label added x8; term declared x3;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Simpleoraggregated Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


